  "scenario": "On a post-surgical step-down unit, the average functional recovery score for recovering patients has slipped about 25% over the past quarter, and the pattern has held across successive admissions. It emerged after a change to the unit's standing medication and fluid protocol. The care team's leading theories are that patients are dehydrated or under-oxygenated, so they favor more fluids and oxygen. Several patients have shown low-grade temperature readings on and off. Routine labs and vitals read broadly within range. The fluid and oxygen orders, medication list, and supportive care are all adjustable within protocol. You have a limited number of experiments; you may measure quantities and apply available interventions, alone or in combination. Determine what is really driving the decline and what to do about it.",
